# Interactive Triage System

## Specs

```yaml
- title: Interactive Triage System
  slug: interactive-triage
  type: feature
  description: |
    Persistent triage metadata system with interactive UI. Triage decisions
    (reasoning, evidence, actions) are stored as TriageRecords in
    project.triage.yaml, surviving inbox item deletion. Supports agent
    triage, user override, action execution, and context export for agent handoff.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        the kspec project has inbox items that need triage
      when: |
        a user or agent initiates the triage workflow
      then: |
        triage decisions are recorded as persistent TriageRecords in
        project.triage.yaml, surviving inbox item deletion
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        an agent triages an inbox item, a user overrides the decision,
        the override is acted on, and the result is exported
      when: |
        the export is generated
      then: |
        the full decision chain (agent recommendation, user override,
        action outcome) is captured with attribution and timestamps

- title: Triage Record Schema
  slug: triage-record-schema
  type: requirement
  parent: "@interactive-triage"
  traits:
    - "@trait-error-guidance"
  description: |
    Zod schema for TriageRecord and TriageFile, stored in
    project.triage.yaml. Follows plan.ts pattern with status lifecycle
    and input schema variant.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        a triage record is created for an inbox item
      when: |
        the record is validated by the Zod schema
      then: |
        it requires _ulid, inbox_ref (source item ULID), item_snapshot
        (text at triage time), status, and created_at
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        a triage decision is recorded
      when: |
        the action field is set
      then: |
        action must be one of promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, or duplicate
    - id: ac-3
      given: |
        a triage record includes a decision
      when: |
        the record is saved
      then: |
        it includes reasoning (string), decided_by (string), and
        optional evidence_refs (array of ref strings)
    - id: ac-4
      given: |
        a user overrides an agent triage decision
      when: |
        the override is recorded
      then: |
        the record stores override_reasoning, override_by, and
        override_at timestamp, preserving the original decision fields
    - id: ac-5
      given: |
        a triage record action is executed
      when: |
        the execution completes
      then: |
        status transitions to acted_on, acted_at timestamp is set, and
        result_ref captures the ref of the created item if applicable
    - id: ac-6
      given: |
        a project.triage.yaml file is loaded
      when: |
        parsed by the Zod schema
      then: |
        it validates as TriageFileSchema with kynetic_triage version
        string and triage array of TriageRecordSchema items
    - id: ac-7
      given: |
        a triage record references an inbox item that has been deleted
      when: |
        the record is loaded
      then: |
        item_snapshot provides the original text so context is preserved
    - id: ac-8
      given: |
        a triage record already exists for a given inbox_ref
      when: |
        a new triage record is attempted for the same inbox_ref
      then: |
        the existing record is updated rather than creating a duplicate
    - id: ac-9
      given: |
        a triage record is mutated (override, act, or update)
      when: |
        the mutation is saved
      then: |
        the updated_at timestamp is set to the current time
  implementation_notes: |
    Create src/schema/triage.ts following plan.ts pattern.
    TriageStatusSchema = z.enum(["pending", "triaged", "acted_on"]).
    TriageActionSchema = z.enum(["promote", "delete", "defer", "spec-gap", "duplicate"]).
    Include updated_at field set on any mutation.
    Enforce inbox_ref uniqueness in save logic (upsert pattern).
    Add load/save in src/parser/yaml.ts: getTriageFilePath, loadTriageRecords, saveTriageRecord.

- title: Triage CLI Commands
  slug: triage-cli-commands
  type: requirement
  parent: "@interactive-triage"
  traits:
    - "@trait-json-output"
    - "@trait-error-guidance"
    - "@trait-semantic-exit-codes"
    - "@trait-filterable-list"
    - "@trait-shadow-commit"
    - "@trait-dry-run"
  description: |
    CLI commands for recording, listing, acting on, overriding, and
    exporting triage decisions. Follows inbox.ts command registration pattern.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage record <inbox-ref> --action promote --reasoning "clear feature request"
      when: |
        the inbox item exists
      then: |
        creates a TriageRecord with item_snapshot from inbox item,
        status triaged, the given action and reasoning, and commits
        to shadow branch
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage list
      when: |
        triage records exist
      then: |
        displays records with ULID prefix, item snapshot (truncated),
        status, action, decided_by, and relative time
    - id: ac-3
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage list --status pending
      when: |
        records with various statuses exist
      then: |
        only records matching the status filter are shown
    - id: ac-4
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref>
      when: |
        the record has status triaged and action promote
      then: |
        executes the promote action (creates task from snapshot),
        transitions record to acted_on with acted_at and result_ref
    - id: ac-5
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref> on a record with action delete
      when: |
        the referenced inbox item still exists
      then: |
        deletes the inbox item without additional confirmation (the
        triage decision serves as prior authorization) and transitions
        record to acted_on
    - id: ac-6
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref> on a record with action defer
      when: |
        the record is triaged
      then: |
        transitions to acted_on with no side effect beyond recording the deferral
    - id: ac-7
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref> on a record with action spec-gap
      when: |
        the record is triaged
      then: |
        creates an observation tagged spec-gap with the item snapshot
        and reasoning, transitions record to acted_on with result_ref
    - id: ac-8
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref> on a record with action duplicate
      when: |
        the record is triaged
      then: |
        deletes the inbox item (prior authorization) and transitions
        record to acted_on
    - id: ac-9
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage start
      when: |
        untriaged inbox items exist
      then: |
        enters interactive mode presenting items one at a time,
        prompting for action and reasoning, creating triage records
        for each, skipping already-triaged items
    - id: ac-10
      given: |
        the user aborts interactive triage mode with Ctrl+C
      when: |
        some items have been triaged
      then: |
        all previously committed triage records are preserved
    - id: ac-11
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage record <ref> with --json flag
      when: |
        the command succeeds
      then: |
        outputs the created triage record as structured JSON
    - id: ac-12
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage override <triage-ref> --action defer --reasoning "not ready yet"
      when: |
        the triage record exists with an existing decision
      then: |
        updates the record with override_reasoning, override_by,
        override_at, and the new action
    - id: ac-13
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage export --format context
      when: |
        triage records exist
      then: |
        outputs a markdown context block per record with item text,
        action, reasoning, decided_by, evidence refs, and outcome
    - id: ac-14
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage export --format json
      when: |
        triage records exist
      then: |
        outputs a JSON array with full TriageRecord objects
    - id: ac-15
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref>
      when: |
        the record has status acted_on (already executed)
      then: |
        returns an error with guidance that the record has already been acted on
    - id: ac-16
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref>
      when: |
        the record has status pending (no decision yet)
      then: |
        returns an error with guidance to record a decision first
    - id: ac-17
      given: |
        user runs kspec triage act <triage-ref> with --dry-run flag
      when: |
        the record has status triaged
      then: |
        shows what action would be taken without executing it
  implementation_notes: |
    Create src/cli/commands/triage.ts following inbox.ts pattern.
    Register via registerTriageCommands(program).
    The act command dispatches on record.action: promote reuses inbox
    promote logic, delete reuses inbox delete logic, spec-gap creates
    observation, duplicate deletes inbox item, defer is a no-op transition.
    Interactive start mode uses readline prompts.
    Override subcommand updates existing record with override fields.
    Export subcommand delegates to shared formatter.

- title: Triage Daemon API
  slug: triage-daemon-api
  type: requirement
  parent: "@interactive-triage"
  traits:
    - "@trait-api-endpoint"
    - "@trait-websocket-protocol"
  description: |
    REST and WebSocket API for triage operations. Elysia routes
    following inbox.ts pattern with pubsub broadcasts.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        a GET request is sent to /api/triage
      when: |
        triage records exist
      then: |
        returns items array and total count, sorted by created_at desc
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        a GET request includes status query parameter
      when: |
        records with various statuses exist
      then: |
        returns only records matching the status filter
    - id: ac-3
      given: |
        a POST request is sent to /api/triage with inbox_ref, action, reasoning
      when: |
        the referenced inbox item exists
      then: |
        creates a TriageRecord with item_snapshot, returns the record,
        and broadcasts triage:updates via WebSocket
    - id: ac-4
      given: |
        a PUT request is sent to /api/triage/:ref with override fields
      when: |
        the triage record exists
      then: |
        stores override_reasoning, override_by, override_at, updates
        action, and broadcasts triage:updates
    - id: ac-5
      given: |
        a PUT request is sent to /api/triage/:ref with act flag
      when: |
        the record has status triaged
      then: |
        executes the action, transitions to acted_on, sets result_ref,
        broadcasts triage:updates
    - id: ac-6
      given: |
        a GET request is sent to /api/triage/export with format parameter
      when: |
        triage records exist
      then: |
        returns context markdown or structured JSON based on format
    - id: ac-7
      given: |
        a POST request references a nonexistent inbox item
      when: |
        the inbox_ref does not resolve
      then: |
        returns 404 with error guidance
    - id: ac-8
      given: |
        a PUT request with act flag targets a record with status acted_on
      when: |
        the record has already been executed
      then: |
        returns 409 conflict with guidance message
    - id: ac-9
      given: |
        a PUT request with act flag targets a record with status pending
      when: |
        no decision has been recorded
      then: |
        returns 422 with guidance to complete triage first
  implementation_notes: |
    Create packages/daemon/src/routes/triage.ts.
    Elysia prefix /api/triage with pubsub injection.
    Topic triage:updates, events: triage_created, triage_updated, triage_acted.
    Register in server.ts alongside existing routes.

- title: Interactive Triage UI
  slug: interactive-triage-ui
  type: requirement
  parent: "@interactive-triage"
  traits:
    - "@trait-websocket-protocol"
  description: |
    Card-based interactive triage mode in the web dashboard.
    One-at-a-time item presentation with action selection,
    reasoning input, and real-time updates.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        the user navigates to the triage page
      when: |
        untriaged inbox items exist
      then: |
        displays a card-based view showing item text, tags, age, and added_by
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        the user views a triage card for an item with an existing agent triage record
      when: |
        the record has status triaged
      then: |
        shows the agent recommended action, reasoning, and evidence refs
    - id: ac-3
      given: |
        the user selects an action and enters reasoning
      when: |
        they submit the decision
      then: |
        creates or updates a triage record via the API and advances to next item
    - id: ac-4
      given: |
        the user disagrees with the agent recommendation
      when: |
        they select a different action with override reasoning
      then: |
        the triage record captures the override with user attribution
    - id: ac-5
      given: |
        the user is in triage mode
      when: |
        they use next/previous navigation
      then: |
        they can browse items without committing decisions, and
        already-triaged items show their decision state
    - id: ac-6
      given: |
        the triage page is open
      when: |
        another client creates or updates a triage record
      then: |
        the view updates in real-time via WebSocket triage:updates topic
    - id: ac-7
      given: |
        the user wants to filter items
      when: |
        they use tag or status filters
      then: |
        the card view shows only matching items with updated progress count
    - id: ac-8
      given: |
        the web UI is in static mode
      when: |
        the user navigates to triage
      then: |
        triage decisions display read-only with action buttons hidden,
        card navigation still works for browsing
  implementation_notes: |
    Create packages/web-ui/src/routes/triage/+page.svelte.
    Card nav with index tracking. Progress bar (triaged/total).
    Action buttons as button row. Textarea for reasoning.
    Subscribe to triage:updates WebSocket topic.
    Add fetchTriage, createTriageRecord, updateTriageRecord to api.ts.

- title: Triage Agent Export
  slug: triage-agent-export
  type: requirement
  parent: "@interactive-triage"
  traits:
    - "@trait-json-output"
  description: |
    Context-rich export of triage decisions for agent handoff.
    Two formats: structured JSON and markdown context block.
    Shared formatter used by both CLI and daemon API.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - id: ac-1
      given: |
        an agent needs context about prior triage decisions
      when: |
        triage export is called with format context
      then: |
        outputs a markdown block per record with item text, action,
        reasoning, decided_by, evidence refs, and outcome
    - id: ac-2
      given: |
        triage export is called with format json
      when: |
        records exist
      then: |
        outputs a JSON array with full TriageRecord objects
    - id: ac-3
      given: |
        triage records include overrides
      when: |
        the export is generated
      then: |
        both original agent decision and user override are included
    - id: ac-4
      given: |
        no triage records exist
      when: |
        export is called
      then: |
        outputs empty result with message indicating no decisions recorded
  implementation_notes: |
    Export formatter in src/lib/triage-export.ts or co-located in CLI command.
    Context format: markdown template with per-item headers.
    JSON format: raw TriageRecord array.
    Shared by CLI (kspec triage export) and API (GET /api/triage/export).
```

## Tasks

derive_from_specs: true

## Implementation Notes

Implementation order follows dependency chain:
1. Schema first (triage-record-schema) — everything depends on types
2. Parser/storage — loadTriageRecords, saveTriageRecord in src/parser/yaml.ts
3. CLI + API + Export can parallel after schema
4. Web UI last — depends on API routes

Key patterns to follow:
- Schema: src/schema/plan.ts (status lifecycle pattern)
- Parser: src/parser/yaml.ts (getXxxFilePath, loadXxx, saveXxx)
- CLI: src/cli/commands/inbox.ts (promote logic reuse)
- Daemon: packages/daemon/src/routes/inbox.ts (Elysia + pubsub)
- Web UI: packages/web-ui/src/routes/inbox/+page.svelte (Svelte 5 reactivity)

Triage skill integration: Update .claude/skills/triage/SKILL.md and docs/inbox.md
to use kspec triage record + kspec triage act instead of directly calling
kspec inbox promote/delete. The skill becomes the orchestrator that creates
persistent triage records, and the user can review/override via web UI.


